The game still works for SKYLINE and C-net and soon with PARAGON.

Setup for C-net:

   Some sysops put games under directorys in pfiles: area.  The spcemp.cfg
has to be on the main pfiles: area then in the config file change to where
you want it to search for data and the rest of it.  I have mine in the
main pfiles: area.  If you want it underr directory games your config line
for that should look like this.

Pfiles:Games/


Then the data will be put under a sub-direcotry called SEDATA.  THere
isn't anything SKYLINE has that C-Net doesn't have.  I made all options
work for both of them.   I can't remember if there is anything to say. If
you have problems then leave me a message about it.

This game cann't be ran at the same time.  The data files will be messed
up so run it exculsive please.  If you want to run it right.


Install:

   Where ever you decide to put it under make a sub-directory called
   SEDATA

    Put SPCEMP.DOC under that.  THat is it.
        SPCEMP.CFG under  PFILES:  THe program checks for it there.

   Files:   Space, Space.ans,  SPace.sky  spacealias.rexx  is for skyline
            only so delete them unless you want extra files around.




